1
00:00:01,450 --> 00:00:10,680
Long ago, Jacob had twelve sons. And the one he loved most of all was young Joseph.

2
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:18,420
Joseph, come here! Father has made you a new coat. Look... all the colours of the rainbow!

3
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,260
Wow, it's beautiful! Thank you, Father!

4
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:27,230
Hmph. Him again. Father gives him all the good things!

5
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:35,210
Brothers, I had a dream! We were tying up bundles of wheat in the field, and all your bundles bowed down to mine!

6
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:41,100
What? You mean WE are going to bow down to YOU? Dream on!

7
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:50,540
Then Joseph dreamed that the sun, the moon and eleven stars all bowed down to him. His brothers were angrier than ever.

8
00:00:53,740 --> 00:01:01,370
One day, the brothers grabbed Joseph's beautiful coat and dropped him into a dry well.

9
00:01:01,870 --> 00:01:03,870
Brothers! Please don't leave me!

10
00:01:05,270 --> 00:01:18,680
Just then some traders came by with their camels. The brothers took twenty pieces of silver and sold Joseph. The traders took him far, far away, to Egypt.

11
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:23,450
My Joseph... my boy is gone...

12
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:35,560
In Egypt, Joseph became a servant. He worked hard and he was honest. But someone told a lie about him, and he was put in prison.

13
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:41,170
Dear God, I didn't do anything wrong. But I know You are still with me.

14
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:48,740
And He was. Even in prison, God was with Joseph.

15
00:01:51,140 --> 00:02:06,730
One night Pharaoh, the king of Egypt, had a strange dream. Seven fat cows came up out of the river. Then came seven skinny cows... and they ate the fat cows right up!

16
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:17,270
Aah! Cows eating cows? Grain eating grain? What does it mean? Somebody tell me!

17
00:02:20,070 --> 00:02:22,560
I hear you can tell what dreams mean?

18
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:27,460
No, Your Majesty, I can't. But God can, and He will tell you.

19
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:38,480
The seven fat cows are seven years with plenty of food. The seven skinny cows are seven years with no food at all. So store up grain in the good years, while you can!

20
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:44,340
How wise! God is with you. From today, you shall be in charge of all Egypt!

21
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:58,930
For seven good years Joseph stored up grain, heaps and heaps of it, like the sand on the seashore.

22
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:11,520
Then the hungry years really came. There was no food anywhere... except in Egypt. So Jacob sent his sons to Egypt to buy grain.

23
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:19,720
My lord, please, sell us a little grain. Our whole family is so hungry.

24
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:29,930
Joseph knew his brothers at once. But they did not know him. And Joseph remembered the dream he had as a boy.

25
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:33,100
Your father... is he well?

26
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:37,930
Brothers, it's me... I am Joseph!

27
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:45,800
J-Joseph? I'm sorry! We did such a terrible thing to you...

28
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:55,630
Don't be afraid, and don't be sad. You meant to hurt me, but God turned it into something good, to save many lives.

29
00:03:58,730 --> 00:04:04,050
Then Joseph brought his father and the whole family to live in Egypt.

30
00:04:04,850 --> 00:04:09,590
Joseph! My boy... I can see you again!

31
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:28,540
In the well, in the prison, in the palace, God was with Joseph all the way. When sad things happen to you, you are not alone either. God can turn bad things into good.
